{"source":"siemens2011.pdf","page":4,"pageWidth":595.276,"pageHeight":793.701,"items":[{"text":"The rationale for dynamic contrast enhanced","rect":[76.5354,714.331,257.1006000000001,723.331],"fontSize":9},{"text":"imaging techniques to assess drug effect in addition","rect":[76.5354,702.9928,285.97440000000006,711.9928],"fontSize":9},{"text":"to standard response assessment is clear. Through","rect":[76.5354,691.6546,277.95990000000006,700.6546],"fontSize":9},{"text":"the analysis of the temporal changes in Hounsfield","rect":[76.5354,680.3163999999999,280.2989999999998,689.3163999999999],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Unit (HU) attenuation in blood vessels and tumor,","rect":[76.5354,668.9781999999999,276.26879999999994,677.9781999999999],"fontSize":9},{"text":"measured from a rapid series of images acquired","rect":[76.5354,657.6399999999999,271.9164,666.6399999999999],"fontSize":9},{"text":"during intravenous administration of conventional","rect":[76.5354,646.3017999999998,279.1614000000002,655.3017999999998],"fontSize":9},{"text":"iodinated contrast agent, DCE-CT can assess the","rect":[76.5354,634.9635999999998,268.9194000000001,643.9635999999998],"fontSize":9},{"text":"vascular support of tumors. Contrast agents","rect":[76.5354,623.6253999999998,253.1010000000001,632.6253999999998],"fontSize":9},{"text":"distribute to the intravascular and extracellular","rect":[76.5354,612.2871999999998,264.5265000000001,621.2871999999998],"fontSize":9},{"text":"compartments and thus can be analyzed using","rect":[76.5354,600.9489999999997,263.9946000000001,609.9489999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"standard kinetic models.","rect":[76.5354,589.6107999999997,174.99,598.6107999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"The measured physiological parameters include:","rect":[303.3066,714.3345999999997,497.2493999999991,723.3345999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"• regional tumor blood flow (blood flow per unit","rect":[303.3066,697.3263999999997,498.529199999999,706.3263999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"volume or mass of tissue)","rect":[310.3932,685.9881999999997,413.13719999999944,694.9881999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"• regional tumor blood volume (the proportion of","rect":[303.3066,668.9799999999997,503.2100999999991,677.9799999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"tissue that is comprised of blood)","rect":[310.3932,657.6408999999996,444.2303999999991,666.6408999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"• blood flow-extraction product (reflecting the rate","rect":[303.3066,640.6326999999997,508.66139999999905,649.6326999999997],"fontSize":9},{"text":"of transfer of contrast agent from the intravascular","rect":[310.3932,629.2944999999996,514.9901999999989,638.2944999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"to extravascular space)","rect":[310.3932,617.9553999999996,402.4991999999996,626.9553999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"• permeability-surface area product.","rect":[303.3066,600.9471999999996,449.2631999999994,609.9471999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Thus both regional perfusion and microvascular","rect":[303.3066,583.9389999999996,495.02549999999917,592.9389999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"changes, reflecting tumor angiogenesis, may be","rect":[303.3066,572.6007999999996,496.6949999999989,581.6007999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"depicted by DCE-CT (Table 1). The information","rect":[303.3066,561.2616999999996,488.94059999999916,570.2616999999996],"fontSize":9},{"text":"provided by the relationship between regional","rect":[303.3066,549.9234999999995,488.79029999999915,558.9234999999995],"fontSize":9},{"text":"blood flow, reflecting oxygen delivery, and regional","rect":[303.3066,538.5843999999995,510.16259999999914,547.5843999999995],"fontSize":9},{"text":"tumor blood volume or permeability-surface area","rect":[303.3066,527.2461999999995,501.3965999999991,536.2461999999995],"fontSize":9},{"text":"potentially reflects the tumor’s adaptation to","rect":[303.3066,515.9070999999994,482.98979999999904,524.9070999999994],"fontSize":9},{"text":"hypoxia, and thus is of clinical relevance.","rect":[303.3066,504.5688999999994,467.696999999999,513.5688999999994],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Tumor type","rect":[80.7874,419.703,129.52240000000003,428.703],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Histological Marker","rect":[180.56770000000003,419.703,264.10569999999984,428.703],"fontSize":9},{"text":"CT parameter","rect":[283.17399999999986,419.703,341.0529999999997,428.703],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Author","rect":[385.7703999999997,419.703,415.45239999999967,428.703],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Year","rect":[488.41179999999963,419.703,507.2487999999996,428.703],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Non-Small Cell Lung","rect":[80.7874,404.26,162.92319999999998,413.26],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Cancer (NSCLC)","rect":[80.7874,392.9209,143.90440000000004,401.9209],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Microvessel Density","rect":[180.5668,404.26,260.1807999999998,413.26],"fontSize":9},{"text":"(MVD)","rect":[180.5668,392.9209,206.50479999999996,401.9209],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Peak enhancement","rect":[283.1812,404.26,360.5271999999998,413.26],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Tateishi et al. [8]","rect":[385.79649999999975,404.26,453.6294999999996,413.26],"fontSize":9},{"text":"2002","rect":[488.41179999999963,404.26,509.5527999999996,413.26],"fontSize":9},{"text":"NSCLC","rect":[80.78739999999999,377.4778,106.7884,386.4778],"fontSize":9},{"text":"MVD, Vascular","rect":[180.5668,377.4778,238.8327999999999,386.4778],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Endothelial Growth","rect":[180.5668,366.1396,258.89560000000006,375.1396],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Factor (VEGF)","rect":[180.5668,354.8005,235.82679999999988,363.8005],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Peak enhancement","rect":[283.1812,377.4778,360.5271999999998,386.4778],"fontSize":9},{"text":"Yi et al. [9]","rect":[385.79649999999975,377.4778,430.40949999999964,386.4778],"fontSize":9},{"text":"2004","rect":[488.4108999999997,377.4778,509.55189999999965,386.4778],"fontSize":9},{"text":"NSCLC","rect":[80.78739999999999,339.3574,106.7884,348.3574],"fontSize":9},{"text":"MVD","rect":[180.5668,3